Kimi Codex Memory

This project includes original and minimally modified prompt templates from OpenAI Codex,
Copyright 2025 OpenAI, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
The upstream NOTICE is preserved in src/kimi_memory/prompts/CODEX-NOTICE.
Pristine templates are in vendor/codex/memories. Runtime read_path_v2,
stage_one_input_v2, stage_one_system_v2 and consolidation_v2 templates are
modified for Kimi session terminology, live notes paths and the available tools.
See docs/upstream.md for pinned source paths, hashes, and deliberate adaptations.
This is an independent integration, not an official OpenAI or Moonshot product.

The authentication bridge includes unmodified OAuth lifecycle and storage sources
from Kimi Code, Copyright (c) 2026 Moonshot AI, under the MIT license.
Original sources/license are in vendor/kimi-oauth; bundled runtime notices are in
src/kimi_memory/native. Build-time bundling also includes proper-lockfile and its
MIT/ISC-licensed dependencies; their licenses accompany the bundle.

The model bridge reuses unmodified Kimi Code low-level streaming requesters,
message codecs, thinking configuration and Kimi protocol traits. The pinned
source files and MIT license are preserved in vendor/kimi-requester. This is
not a bundled Kimi application or coding agent. MODEL-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES in
src/kimi_memory/native covers bundled SDK and transport dependencies.

Native plugin runtimes embed CPython and the unmodified PyInstaller bootloader.
Their redistribution terms, including the PyInstaller bootloader exception,
are included in each platform runtime's licenses directory.
